Quiz Translation & Solution Breakdown (Week 3, Lesson 2)
Question 1
Korean: DNC(Direct Numerical Control)의 설명으로 옳은 것은?

English: Which of the following is a correct description of DNC (Direct Numerical Control)?

Options:

여러 대의 NC기계를 한 대의 컴퓨터에 연결시켜 제어 (Controlling multiple NC machines connected to a single computer)

NC 공작기계 내에 저장되어 있는 표준부프로그램(subroutine) (Standard subroutine stored inside an NC machine tool)

컴퓨터(마이크로프로세서)를 내장한 NC공작기계 (An NC machine tool with a built-in computer/microprocessor)

컴퓨터의 핵심기능을 수행하는 중앙 연산 처리장치 (Central processing unit performing core computer functions)

Correct Answer: ① (Index 0)

Context/Rationale: DNC refers to a system architecture where a single central computer connects to and controls multiple NC/CNC machine tools simultaneously. An NC machine tool with a built-in computer is CNC, while option 4 describes a CPU.

Question 2
Korean: 다음 중 일반적인 공구경로 시뮬레이션을 통해 파트 프로그래머가 직접 시각적으로 확인하기 어려운 것은?

English: Which of the following is difficult for a part programmer to directly verify visually through standard tool path simulation?

Options:

공구가 공작물의 필요한 부분까지 제거하는지의 여부 (Whether the tool removes the necessary portion of the workpiece)

공구가 어떤 클램프(clamp)나 고정구(fixture)와 충돌하는지의 여부 (Whether the tool collides with clamps or fixtures)

공구가 포켓(pocket)의 바닥이나 측면, 리브(lib)를 관통하여 지나가는지의 여부 (Whether the tool passes through/gouges pocket floors, walls, or ribs)

공구에 어떤 힘이 가해지며, 공구경로가 공구수명에 효율적인지의 여부 (What forces are applied to the tool and whether the tool path is efficient for tool life)

Correct Answer: ④ (Index 3)

Context/Rationale: Visual 3D tool path simulations allow programmers to inspect geometric aspects (stock removal, clearance, fixture collision, and gouging). Dynamic cutting forces, thermal effects, and tool-life wear cannot be directly observed from simple visual simulation.

Question 3
Korean: 다음 그림의 A 점에서 B 점까지 가공하는 프로그램으로 옳은 것은?

English: Which program block correctly commands the machining of the arc from point A to point B in the given diagram?

Diagram Parameters:

Start point A=(50,5), End point B=(10,5).

Curved path travels along the top semicircle from A to B.

Counterclockwise (CCW) direction around center (30,5)→ G03.

Incremental distance (G91): ΔX=10−50=−40, ΔY=0.

Center vector from start point A: I=30−50=−20, J=0.

Options:

G91 G03 X-30. I10. ;

G91 G03 X-40. I-20. ;

G91 G03 X10. Y5. J-20. ;

G91 G03 X10. Y5. J-10. ;

Correct Answer: ② (Index 1): G91 G03 X-40. I-20. ;

Question 4
Korean: CNC 프로그램의 보조기능에 해당되지 않는 것은?

English: Which of the following does NOT correspond to an auxiliary (miscellaneous) function in a CNC program?

Options:

절삭유 공급 여부 (Coolant supply on/off) → M08, M09

프로그램 시작지령 (Program start command)

주축회전 방향 결정 (Determining spindle rotation direction) → M03, M04

보조프로그램 호출 (Calling a subprogram) → M98

Correct Answer: ② (Index 1)

Context/Rationale: M codes control auxiliary operations like coolant, spindle direction, tool changes, and program stops/ends (M02/M30). Starting a program is initiated by the program number address (O) and preparatory functions (G), not an auxiliary M code.

