Alright, now here is the week 6 lesson 1 quiz snapshot

I have analyzed the snapshot for Week 6, Lesson 1 and referenced your course context.

This quiz reinforces concepts surrounding the CAD/CAM workflow, system terminology, standard file formats, and auxiliary M-codes. Here is the breakdown:

Q1 (Multiple Machine Control): A system connecting a central computer to control multiple CNC machines simultaneously is a DNC (Direct/Distributed Numerical Control).

Q2 (Neutral File Formats): DXF, IGES, and STEP are all standard cross-platform CAD file formats. GUI stands for Graphical User Interface (like menus and buttons) and is not a file format.

Q3 (CAM Workflow): The standard CAM progression is: Part Program → Generate CL (Cutter Location) Data → Run through Post-Processor → Output final NC Code.

Q4 (M-Code Error): M09 is the command to turn coolant OFF, not ON. (M08 turns it ON).

