Alright, here's the week 6 lesson 2 quiz snapshot

I have processed the snapshot for Week 6, Lesson 2.

This quiz blends general CAD/CAM theory with specific CNC programming syntax, creating a well-rounded review. Here is the context mapping:

Q1 (CAD/CAM Workflow): This is a re-test of the concept from Week 5. The correct sequence is: Shape Modeling (가) → Tool Path Generation/CL Data (나) → Tool Path Verification/Simulation (다) → Post-processing (라) → Machining Conditions Definition (마).

Q2 (Coordinate Systems): A fundamental rule in machine tool coordinates is that the Z-axis is always parallel to the main spindle (주축), regardless of whether it's a lathe or a milling machine. Option 3 is incorrect because on a lathe (선반), the X-axis determines the diameter and moves perpendicular to the rotational axis, not the direction of the tool's primary movement.

Q3 (Addresses): This is a recall question for the basic alphabet of CNC.

G = Preparatory function (준비기능)

F = Feed function (이송기능)

S = Spindle function (주축기능)

T = Tool function (공구기능)

Therefore, T being labeled as "Dwell/Pause function" (휴지기능) is incorrect. Dwell is actually handled by G04 (using P or X for time).

Q4 (Fixed Cycles - P Address): In fixed cycle (canned cycle) hole machining (like G82 or G89), the address P is universally used to command a Dwell time (휴지시간) at the bottom of the hole.

