This is Week 7 Lesson 1 quiz snapshot

I have analyzed the snapshot for Week 7, Lesson 1 and referenced the foundational CNC context.

This quiz tests the mechanical components related to precision (backlash), the specific functions of preparatory G-codes (like G80), program structure (N-codes vs O-codes), and a review of the Open Loop servo system.

Here is the breakdown of the new questions:

Q1 (Backlash): Backlash (백 래시) in CNC machine tools is the mechanical play or lost motion caused by clearance between the threads of the lead screw and the nut. Modern CNC machines use Ball Screws (볼 스크류) to drastically reduce this directly.

Q2 (Sequence Numbers): Sequence numbers (N-codes) are used to label blocks for easy searching and don't need to be on every line. However, they are NOT used to distinguish separate programs from each other—that is the job of the Program Number (O-code).

Q3 (G80 Code): In the initialization block G40 G49 G80, G40 cancels radius compensation, G49 cancels length compensation, and G80 cancels fixed/canned cycles (고정 사이클 취소).

Q4 (Servo Systems): A system that relies entirely on input pulses with no detector or feedback circuit (검출기나 피드백 회로가 없으므로) is an Open Loop System (개방 회로 방식).

