This quiz shifts gears to a broader view of manufacturing systems and a review of coordinate programming concepts. Here is the context mapping:

Q1 (Control Systems): The standard CNC control systems are Open Loop (개방회로), Closed Loop (폐쇄회로), Semi-Closed Loop (반폐쇄회로), and Hybrid (하이브리드). "Semi-open loop" (반개방 제어방식) is a fabricated term and does not exist.

Q2 (Coordinate Commands): In CNC programming, positions are commanded either absolutely (G90) or incrementally (G91). Mixed commands are also used. However, "Machine Origin Command Method" (기계원점지령 방식) is not a method for specifying tool movement coordinates; G28 is a specific action (return to reference point), not a coordinate plotting method.

Q3 (Machining Plans): Before programming, a CAM operator must determine the machining sequence, select tools, choose the specific CNC machine, and figure out how to clamp/fixture the workpiece. "Selection of position detection method" (위치 검출 방법의 선정) is a hardware design choice (e.g., choosing between semi-closed or closed loop), decided by the machine manufacturer, not the programmer.

Q4 (FMS Characteristics): Flexible Manufacturing Systems (FMS) are designed for adaptability. They reduce labor costs, simplify inventory, and easily handle process changes. However, they are fundamentally designed for High-mix, low-volume production (다품종 소량생산), not "mass production of a single item" (단품종 대량생산).

